---
title: "Go settings over Bluetooth"
nav_title: Configure
description: "Change skyBlip Go settings over Bluetooth from Chrome or Edge: aircraft type, callsign, own ICAO, units and alarm. Approve each change on the device."
updated_on: "2026-11-11"
---
<% content_for :stylesheets, area_stylesheet_link_tags("manage") %>
<% settings = {
     legend: "Settings on the device",
     units: "Units",
     unit_names: { nautical: "Nautical: NM and kt", metric: "Metric: km and km/h" },
     alarm_enabled: "Alarm sound",
     alarm_volume: "Alarm volume",
     volume_names: { off: "Off", soft: "Soft", loud: "Loud" },
     save: "Save",
     reset: "Back to defaults",
     default: "Default: %{value}",
     on: "on",
     off: "off",
     none: "none",
     confirm_set: "Allow the change: the glass says SETTINGS, press twice."
   } %>
<% capture = {
     legend: "Diagnostics capture on a skyBlip Bravo",
     lede: "Bravo has no screen, so its capture is armed from here. It records what the unit hears and decides, for us to read with you after a flight.",
     profile: "Capture",
     profile_names: { full: "Full: every subject", power_run: "Power run: power and duty", flight_run: "Flight run: power and duty, with the flight clock running" },
     arm: "Arm",
     stop: "Stop the capture",
     confirm: "Allow it on Bravo: its lamp blinks green fast, press the button twice."
   } %>

<section id="settings">
  <p class="kicker">skyBlip Go</p>
  <h1>Its settings, from this page, over Bluetooth.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The page reads the settings the device holds, shows which differ from the
    ones it ships on, and changes them, each change asked on the glass.
    Nothing is asked while the device is flying.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    New firmware is on <%= link_to_page "update", label: "the update page" %>,
    and the device stays connected from one page to the other.
  </p>

  <%= render layout: "shared/manage", locals: {
        unsupported: "This browser has no Web Bluetooth, so this page cannot reach the device. Use Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android. Safari, Firefox, and every browser on an iPhone or an iPad lack it.",
        connect: "Connect",
        disconnect: "Disconnect",
        connecting: "Your browser lists the devices in range: pick skyBlip Go followed by its address.",
        device: "Device",
        firmware: "Running",
        battery: "Battery",
        charging: "charging",
        flight: { label: "Flight", ground: "on the ground", airborne: "airborne", unknown: "not yet known" },
        settings:
      } do %>
    <%= render "shared/manage_settings", settings: %>
    <%= render "shared/manage_capture", capture: %>
  <% end %>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">Before you start</h2>

  <ul class="points">
    <li>Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android</li>
    <li>The device on the ground. Older firmware also waits for a GPS fix</li>
    <li>No other app holding the device&rsquo;s settings</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">What happens</h2>

  <h3>What it holds, <span class="highlight">beside what it ships on</span>.</h3>
  <p class="lede">
    Once connected, the page reads the aircraft type, the callsign, the units,
    the alarm and the own ICAO address from the device, and asks the firmware
    for the values a new unit ships on. A setting that differs from those says
    so under its field.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    Save sends only what you changed. Back to defaults sends the firmware&rsquo;s
    own values for what differs. Either way the glass says
    <span class="mono">SETTINGS</span> and lists each change in the words of
    its own menu, such as <span class="mono">CALLSIGN F-JXYZ</span>, up to four
    rows: press twice, and the page reads the settings back from the device.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    The radar&rsquo;s range and plot are set on the device&rsquo;s own menu,
    and the page leaves them as they are.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    The aeroplane at the centre of the radar is drawn on
    <%= link_to "its own page", briefing_ownship_path %>, one per aircraft type,
    a glider for a glider. The device shows the light aircraft for every type
    until it learns to take a drawing over Bluetooth.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="modules">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The page says</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Saved</th><td data-manage-word="saved">The device stored the settings, and the form shows them as the device read them back.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">settings: prior</th><td data-manage-word="settings_prior">Your settings are the ones from before the last update: what you changed while the newer firmware ran stayed with it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">settings: defaults</th><td data-manage-word="settings_defaults">The stored settings could not be read, so the device runs on its defaults. Check the callsign and the aircraft type before you fly.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">no address</th><td data-manage-word="not_activated">This unit is not activated yet, so it neither transmits nor receives. Give it its serial on the activation page, skyblip.eu/activate.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Capture armed</th><td data-manage-word="capture_armed">Bravo records the capture you chose, and its lamp winks twice every 3 s until it stops. It keeps recording across a flight. Stop it from this page on the ground, or switch the unit off.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Capture stopped</th><td data-manage-word="capture_stopped">Bravo closed the capture, and its lamp winks once again.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">When it says no</h2>

  <p class="lede">
    Every refusal comes with a reason, and the page puts it in the words below.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="modules">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The device answers</th><th>What it means, and what to do</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th class="mono">in_flight</th><td data-manage-word="in_flight">The device says it is flying. Try again once it has landed. Older firmware also says so until its first GPS fix since it was switched on: take it where it sees the sky and wait for the fix.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">low_power</th><td data-manage-word="low_power">The battery is critical, and the device does not write its settings on a cell that might not finish. Charge it, then try again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">expired</th><td data-manage-word="expired">Nobody answered the question on the glass within thirty seconds, so the device dropped it. Try again, and press twice when the glass asks.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">cancelled</th><td data-manage-word="cancelled">The device said no: one press refuses the question. After a refused question, the device asks nothing more from this connection: disconnect and connect again before you try again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">prompt_pending</th><td data-manage-word="prompt_pending">The glass is already asking a question this connection sent. Answer it on the device, or wait up to thirty seconds for it to go, then try again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">refused_on_device</th><td data-manage-word="refused_on_device">One press on the device refused a question from this connection, so the device asks nothing more from it. Disconnect and connect again, then try again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">small_mtu</th><td data-manage-word="small_mtu">The answer did not fit the link: this phone or browser kept Bluetooth&rsquo;s smallest packet size, 20 bytes. Disconnect and connect again. If it happens again, update the browser and the phone, or connect from another phone or a computer with Chrome or Edge.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">claimed</th><td data-manage-word="claimed">Another app holds this device&rsquo;s settings. Disconnect it or close it, then connect again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">capturing</th><td data-manage-word="capturing">A capture already runs on Bravo. Stop it first, then arm the one you want.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">not_capturing</th><td data-manage-word="not_capturing">No capture runs on Bravo, so there is nothing to stop.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">no_storage</th><td data-manage-word="no_storage">Bravo found no memory to record a capture in. Tell us, with its firmware version.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">unknown_command</th><td data-manage-word="unknown_command">The firmware on the device is older than this page and does not know the question. Update it on <%= link_to_page "update", label: "the update page" %>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th class="mono">anything else</th><td data-manage-word="refused">The device refused, with a reason this page does not know:</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">When the page stops</h2>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="modules">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The page says</th><th>What it means, and what to do</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>No Web Bluetooth</th><td data-manage-word="no_bluetooth">This browser has no Web Bluetooth. Use Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android. Safari, Firefox, and every browser on an iPhone or an iPad lack it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Not a skyBlip</th><td data-manage-word="not_skyblip">The device you picked has no settings service: it is not a skyBlip, or its firmware predates settings over Bluetooth.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Link lost</th><td data-manage-word="link_lost">The link dropped. Bring the device closer and connect again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>No answer</th><td data-manage-word="timeout">The device stopped answering. Disconnect and connect again.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Refused</th><td data-manage-word="smp">The device refused with an error this page does not know:</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Anything else</th><td data-manage-word="failed">Something failed on the way:</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <p>
    <%= link_to_page "update", class: "cta cta--previous" %>
  </p>
</section>
